  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Michael Cotter founded Park Developments, which entered the Irish property market in 1962 and grew into one of Dublin's leading private builders. The company established its scale through suburban housing, delivering thousands of homes before extending into offices, retail parks and industrial property. Cotter led projects including The Gallops in Leopardstown, Mount Saint Anne's in Milltown and The Park Carrickmines.\n\nPark Developments survived the Irish property crash and returned to large residential and commercial schemes. Its later work includes Clay Farm, The Reflector and continuing logistics development in northwest Dublin. Cotter now serves as chairman alongside a professional chief executive and family directors. The group has built more than 13,500 homes and remains active across housing, offices, retail and logistics property.",
    "html": "<p>Michael Cotter founded Park Developments, which entered the Irish property market in 1962 and grew into one of Dublin's leading private builders. The company established its scale through suburban housing, delivering thousands of homes before extending into offices, retail parks and industrial property. Cotter led projects including The Gallops in Leopardstown, Mount Saint Anne's in Milltown and The Park Carrickmines.</p>\r\n<p>Park Developments survived the Irish property crash and returned to large residential and commercial schemes. Its later work includes Clay Farm, The Reflector and continuing logistics development in northwest Dublin. Cotter now serves as chairman alongside a professional chief executive and family directors. The group has built more than 13,500 homes and remains active across housing, offices, retail and logistics property.</p>\r\n",
